cff-version: 1.2.0
# The released tables are deposited at Zenodo. The DOI below is the version
# DOI, which cites this release; the concept DOI under identifiers resolves to
# the latest version. The tables are regenerated by the pipeline and are not
# tracked in this repository, so a copy regenerated here is cited by the commit
# that produced it.
message: "If you use the released data tables, cite them as below."
title: "Bedaquiline and clofazimine MIC effect tables for Rv0678, pepQ and atpE variants in Mycobacterium tuberculosis, from the CRyPTIC Consortium Dataset v3.4.0"
abstract: >-
  Twelve tables quantifying how mutations in the Rv0678 and MmpL5 efflux axis
  shift bedaquiline and clofazimine minimum inhibitory concentrations, with a
  readable report beside each table carrying the same figures and the counts
  they rest on. Every figure derives from the CRyPTIC Consortium Dataset v3.4.0
  through the pipeline in the repository named below. atlas_evidence.csv holds
  one row per distinct mutation in Rv0678, pepQ and atpE carried by a solo
  isolate, with its isolate and cluster counts, the sites and sublineages it
  spans, and its resistant and censored counts for each drug; where the
  independent evidence supports one, a row carries the shift in fitted mean
  log2 MIC against the reference group, with an interval from resampling
  clusters, and a row without one records why it is withheld. The other tables
  carry fitted group means and shifts by variant class, the resistant isolates
  no variant in the cohort accounts for and how that fraction moves as genes
  are admitted to the explaining set, shifts for variants detected in a
  minority of reads, four genotype rules as tests for resistance at every
  concentration both plate designs determine, twenty tests of ten further
  genes, HGVS names for the per-variant rows, and the WHO second-edition
  catalogue measured on this cohort. MICs are interval-censored readings on a
  doubling series, so group means are fitted by maximum likelihood over the
  censoring intervals and intervals come from resampling clonal clusters
  rather than isolates. docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md defines every column.
  Resistance in this collection is concentrated at one site by design, so no
  count in these tables is a prevalence estimate.
